PMT = FV / (((1 + r/n)^(n*t) - 1) / (r/n))


Where:

PMT = Payment per period (quarterly deposit we need to find)

FV = Future value of the annuity (the amount Mrs. Hilton wants to save, which is $10,000)

r = Annual interest rate (5 percent, or 0.05 as a decimal)

n = Number of times the interest is compounded per year (quarterly compounding means four times a year)

t = Time the money is invested, in years (10 years)


